erence/subscriptions-35","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#process-an-unsubscribe-from-your-own-page","content":"Process an unsubscribe from your own page"},"5180":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-36","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#one-click-unsubscribe-rfc-8058","content":"One-click unsubscribe (RFC 8058)"},"5181":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-37","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#related","content":"Related"},"5182":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-38","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#subscriptions-api","content":"The Subscriptions API is the one place to change who receives which mail. Use it from your own application to build newsletter signups, a preference page inside your product, or server-side opt-outs. Every call applies the same rules as NorthRelay's hosted forms, unsubscribe links and preference centre, and fires the same webhooks."},"5183":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-39","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#subscriptions-api","content":"For a walkthrough of how the pieces fit together, see the Mailing Lists guide."},"5184":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-40","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"Term"},"5185":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-41","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"What it is"},"5186":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-42","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"Managed with"},"5187":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-43","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"**List**"},"5188":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-44","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"An audience you send campaigns to. A contact is either a member or not."},"5189":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-45","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"`/contacts/lists`"},"5190":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-46","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"**Topic**"},"5191":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-47","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"A category of mail a recipient can opt out of (for example \"Product updates\"). Stored as a suppression group. A member row in a topic means the address **opted out** of that topic."},"5192":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-48","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"`/suppression-groups`"},"5193":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-49","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"**Global unsubscribe**"},"5194":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-50","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"The recipient wants no marketing mail at all. The contact status becomes `UNSUBSCRIBED` and an account-level suppression with reason `Unsubscribe` is added."},"5195":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-51","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"This API"},"5196":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-52","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"Rules the API enforces for you:"},"5197":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-53","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"Subscribing to a topic means removing the recipient's opt-out for it. Opting out of a topic also removes the recipient from every list tagged with that topic."},"5198":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-54","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"Unsubscribing from a list keeps the membership history (the membership is marked removed). Removing a member as the list owner deletes it (see list members)."},"5199":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-55","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"Someone who unsubscribed is never re-added silently. You must pass `\"resubscribe\": true`, and you should only do so after fresh consent."},"5200":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-56","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"Bounce, complaint and manual suppressions are never lifted by a subscribe call."},"5201":{"id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions-57","page_id":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api-reference/subscriptions#concepts","content":"Contacts with status `COMPLAINED` or `CLEANED` cannot be resubscribed."},"